meta {
  name: Health - secrets
  type: http
  seq: 0
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/health/secrets
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Shows whether each Key Vault secret resolved, its length, and a SHA-256
  fingerprint - never the value itself.

  The fingerprint matches the one provision.ps1 prints. If they differ, the vault
  and the database have drifted apart and -RotatePasswords resyncs both.

  Also echoes Sandbox:Environment, SqlServer and Database, which is worth checking
  first: a wrong database name surfaces as "Login failed for user" rather than
  anything about the database, because contained-user authentication happens
  inside the target database.
}
